<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- Deliberately NOT sandboxed, and deliberately empty.

	     The App Sandbox is inherited by child processes, so with it on the
	     local shell opens inside Séance's own container: $HOME is the
	     container, everything outside it is unreadable, and zsh cannot take
	     control of the terminal ("can't set tty pgrp") — which costs job
	     control, so ^C reaches the shell instead of the command it is
	     running. A terminal that can neither see your files nor interrupt a
	     command is not a terminal. Séance ships as an unsigned/ad-hoc GitHub
	     release and never goes through App Review, so nothing requires the
	     sandbox.

	     What that costs, stated plainly: a compromise of Séance — or of any
	     dependency it pulls in — now reaches everything the user can reach
	     rather than one container, and the SSH keys and vault this app holds
	     are exactly what such a compromise would be after. Putting
	     com.apple.security.app-sandbox back is a one-line change, and
	     SandboxMigration keeps working either way.

	     Everything that used to be here went with it, because all of it is
	     sandbox-only and inert without it: network.client, network.server,
	     files.user-selected.read-write, files.bookmarks.app-scope, and the
	     ~/.ssh read-only temporary exception. Identity files are simply read
	     now; IdentityFileBookmarks already falls back to the plain path when
	     a security-scoped bookmark won't resolve, so it needed no change and
	     the native ~/.ssh-visible file picker still works.

	     Still no keychain-access-groups, for the original reason: it is a
	     RESTRICTED entitlement macOS refuses to honor on ad-hoc ("sign to run
	     locally") builds, and the app then won't launch at all. The keystore
	     plugin targets the legacy login keychain instead
	     (MacOsOptions(usesDataProtectionKeychain: false) in
	     secure_master_key.dart), which needs no entitlement. -->
</dict>
</plist>
